# checkoutpay — private repo reminder

After any successful `git push` to **amithyone/checkoutpay** (or when the user asks to push):

1. Tell the user to confirm the repo is **Private** on GitHub.
2. Link: https://github.com/amithyone/checkoutpay/settings → **General** → **Danger zone** → **Change repository visibility** → **Private**.

Do this every time after a push completes, even if they did not ask. One short sentence is enough unless they are deploying.

Project git hooks (after `scripts/setup-git-hooks.sh`) also print a terminal reminder on push.
